---
description: Обновить установленный пакет ITL workflow
agent: code
---

Use this command only from the `master` worktree. It updates ITL workflow and AI rules files, regenerates the active client's commands, and commits only updater-owned tracked changes. It does not push.

Run the helper from the current project directory:

If the agent shell tool supports `timeout_ms`, use `timeout_ms >= 3900000` so the outer shell outlives the 3600-second Designer limit. If the Designer limit is higher, raise the outer timeout too. Do not use `120000 ms` or other short values.

```powershell
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\.agents\skills\1c-workflow\scripts\run-itl-command.ps1 -- -Action update-workflow
```

If the helper reports a dirty tracked Git worktree, stop and ask the developer to commit or remove the changes, then retry. On success with a non-empty `userReport`, return exactly that Russian Markdown report with no introduction, paraphrase, or `console.log` read. On failure, read only the last 80 lines of `logPath`. Do not run this command from `itldev/*`; development branches update separately through `/itl-refresh`.
